<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: Czech Skoda 1996 uncons. loss narrows.</title>
<headline>Czech Skoda 1996 uncons. loss narrows.</headline>
<dateline>PRAGUE 1997-07-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 1996 audited unconsolidated loss of the Czech engineering holding company Skoda a.s. narrowed to 190.281 million crowns from a loss of 294.575 million crowns in 1995, the company said in a statement.</p>
<p>A company spokesman said the figures, under Czech accounting standards, were only for the parent holding company and did not include any results from subsidiaries.  </p>
<p>   after-tax result (czk million)   190.281 loss   vs  294.575 loss</p>
<p>   pre-tax result		   221.658 loss   vs  291.074 loss</p>
<p>   sales of own goods /services 966.865	  vs  883.272</p>
<p>   sales of other goods	    65.243	  vs  850.313</p>
<p>   result/financial operations  258.523 loss   vs  173.424 loss</p>
<p>   result/regular operations    174.014 loss   vs  217.354 loss</p>
<p>---------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>   paid in capital	     11,356.776	  vs  11,555.327</p>
<p>   basic capital		  9,479.710	  vs   9,479.710</p>
<p>   capital funds		  1,629.718	  vs   1,630.495</p>
<p>   funds from profit		731.771	  vs     739.265</p>
<p>   long-term obligations	1,387.636	  vs   1,471.963</p>
<p>   short-term obligations	 695.820	  vs   1,190.613</p>
<p>   bank credit		    1,658.007	  vs   1,247.595</p>
<p>     long-term credit	     705.374	  vs     841.916</p>
<p>     regular operating credit   474.193	  vs     405.679</p>
<p>     other short-term financing 478.440	  vs	 ---</p>
<p>   net assets		    15,346.713	  vs  15,594.537</p>
<p>Note: The full company name is Skoda a.s., a heavy engineering holding company based in Plzen, no longer affiliated with the car maker Skoda Automobilova a.s..</p>
<p>Skoda a.s. said it expected to release consolidated 1996 results sometime next week.</p>
<p>-- Prague Newsroom, 420-2-2423-0003</p>
</text>
